{
  "esm": "1.0.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "OpenAQ",
    "description": "OpenAQ regridding model — the coupler half of the openaq loader+regridding-model split (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7; bead esm-3nc.5). Exposes ground-based air quality monitoring observations (PM2.5, PM10, O3, NO2, SO2, CO, BC, PM1, NO, NOx) on the simulation's target grid for coupling into EarthSciML systems.\n\nStructure (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6):\n  1. It declares the pure-I/O loader (components/earthsci_data/openaq_loader.esm) as the subsystem `obs` via {\"ref\": \"./openaq_loader.esm\"}. Loader fields are referenced as obs.<var> (e.g. obs.pm25).\n  2. Reprojection: OpenAQ's station coordinates are geographic (longlat/WGS84), so the coordinate transform is the longlat IDENTITY (ESD reprojection/longlat.esm, esd-47z.1) — selected by convention from the loader's native geographic crs (recorded in the loader metadata, since this points loader resolves its native grid at runtime and carries no formal GDD `grid`); a no-op for unprojected station coordinates.\n  3. Regridding (per variable, RFC §5.2): every variable is a scattered point field → cell-averaging regridder (ESD regridding/point_cell_average_regrid.esm, esd-47z.4): the source stations falling within each target cell are bin-averaged, and a target cell containing no station is filled with `missing_value`. Declared in the `regrid` block.\n\nThis model re-exposes the representative parameter pm25 at the model top level (OpenAQ.pm25, expression obs.pm25) to preserve the pre-migration coupling interface. One OpenAQ instantiation covers one parameter; other instantiations use the respective variable name (pm10, o3, no2, so2, co, bc, pm1, no, nox), all available as obs.<var> and all configured in `regrid`.\n\nMigrated from EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/openaq.jl:595 (OpenAQ constructor, esm-mfi7); split into pure loader + regridding model by esm-3nc.5.",
    "tags": [
      "earthsci_data",
      "air_quality",
      "observations",
      "monitoring_stations",
      "hourly",
      "regridding_model",
      "point_observations",
      "longlat"
    ],
    "created": "2026-06-25T00:00:00Z",
