  "data_sources": {
    "OpenAQ_obs": {
      "kind": "points",
      "source": {
        "url_template": "https://openaq-data-archive.s3.amazonaws.com/records/csv.gz/locationid={location_id}/year={date:%Y}/month={date:%m}/location-{location_id}-{date:%Y%m%d}.csv.gz"
      },
      "temporal": {
        "start": "2016-01-01T00:00:00Z",
        "end": "2099-12-31T23:59:59Z",
        "file_period": "P1D",
        "frequency": "PT1H",
        "records_per_file": "auto",
        "time_variable": "datetime"
      },
      "reference": {
        "citation": "OpenAQ. OpenAQ Data Archive. Open-source global air quality data aggregation platform. https://openaq.org/",
        "url": "https://openaq.org/"
      },
      "metadata": {
        "tags": [
          "air_quality",
          "observations",
          "monitoring_stations",
          "hourly",
          "point_observations"
        ],
        "native_crs": {
          "projection": "longlat",
          "datum": "WGS84",
          "proj4": "+proj=longlat +datum=WGS84 +no_defs",
          "note": "Geographic (unprojected) coordinate reference of the station coordinates. Recorded here for provenance because this points loader omits the formal GDD `grid` block (the native point set is resolved at runtime via station discovery). The regridding model (openaq.esm) selects the longlat IDENTITY reprojection by convention from this projection and bins the stations into target cells with the cell-averaging regridder (ESD regridding/point_cell_average_regrid.esm, esd-47z.4). Migrated from the loader's former DataLoaderSpatial block (crs '+proj=longlat +datum=WGS84 +no_defs', grid_type 'unstructured', staggering lon/lat 'center')."
        },
        "unit_conversion_note": "Raw CSV 'value' is reported in µg/m³ (the per-record source unit is carried in the CSV 'unit' column). The runtime scales each variable to its declared `units` (kg/m³) via unit_scale/to_unit at load time (1 µg/m³ = 1×10⁻⁹ kg/m³). The pre-migration explicit numeric `unit_conversion: 1e-9` factor is dropped: under the ESS DataLoaderVariable schema `unit_conversion` is oneOf[number, Expression] and Expression itself admits a number literal, so a bare numeric factor is ambiguous and rejected at load; the conversion is instead expressed by the target `units` declaration (matching the canonical ESS points-loader fixture tests/fixtures/data_loaders/openaq.esm, which declares target units and relies on runtime unit_scale with no explicit factor).",
        "earthscidata_source": "src/openaq.jl::OpenAQFileSet",
        "s3_mirror": "https://openaq-data-archive.s3.amazonaws.com",
        "api_endpoint": "https://api.openaq.org/v3",
        "station_discovery": "runtime (OpenAQ API v3 /locations endpoint — requires OPENAQ_API_KEY env var or api_key constructor argument; results cached to $EARTHSCIDATADIR/openaq_stations/{parameter}_{bbox}.json; no API key needed for S3 data download)",
        "file_format": "gzip-compressed CSV (.csv.gz)",
        "csv_columns": "location_id,sensor_id,location,datetime,lat,lon,parameter,unit,value",
        "datetime_format": "ISO8601 with timezone offset (e.g. 2024-01-15T12:00:00+00:00); runtime converts all timestamps to UTC before aggregation",
        "valid_parameters": [
          "pm25",
          "pm10",
          "o3",
          "no2",
          "so2",
          "co",
          "bc",
          "pm1",
          "no",
          "nox"
        ],
        "former_regridding": "The pre-migration data_loaders.regridding block declared fill_value 0.0 and extrapolation 'clamp'. fill_value migrates to the model regrid blocks' `missing_value` 0.0 (cell_average kernel); extrapolation 'clamp' has no analogue in the cell-averaging kernel (which fills empty cells with missing_value rather than extrapolating) and is dropped (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §5.2).",
        "location_id_note": "The {location_id} URL substitution is a custom (non-standard) template variable resolved at runtime from the station list returned by station discovery. Each station in the discovered list produces one URL per day in the simulation time span.",
        "data_availability": "Coverage varies by region and time period. Data starting ~2016 in many regions. Missing S3 files (HTTP 404) are treated as no-data (no error); the corresponding station-day contributes zero readings to its grid cell."
      }
    }
  },
  "models": {
    "OpenAQ": {
      "reference": {
        "notes": "source_ref: EarthSciData.jl@830435a065f27e99f10bba91107ca1730322cc6b:src/openaq.jl:595\n\nThis is the regridding-model half of the pure-IO loader migration (RFC pure-io-data-loaders §6/§7, bead esm-3nc.5). The pre-migration openaq.esm carried both the coupler model AND a co-located data_loaders.OpenAQ_obs block (with the now-removed `spatial` and `regridding` sub-blocks). That loader is now the pure-I/O file components/earthsci_data/openaq_loader.esm, referenced here as subsystem `obs`.\n\nUpstream constructor OpenAQ(parameter, domaininfo; api_key, station_filter, fill_value=0.0, name=:OpenAQ, stream=true, spatial_interp=:linear) created an MTK System with:\n  - @parameters: lon (rad), lat (rad) from domaininfo pvars (surface point observations: 2-D [x, y], no vertical level).\n  - One observed equation via create_interp_equation(itp, \"\", t, t_ref, [x, y]; spatial_interp) where itp = DataSetInterpolator{dt}(FileSetWithRegridder(fs, copy_regridder), parameter, ...) and fs = OpenAQFileSet(parameter, starttime, endtime, bbox; grid_lon_edges, grid_lat_edges, ...). The variable name matches the parameter string (e.g. pm25(t)). These are now provided by the loader subsystem `obs` (obs.<var>); pm25 is re-exposed as a model observed (expression obs.pm25) to preserve the OpenAQ.pm25 coupling interface.\n  - discrete_events: build_interp_event fires hourly to reload S3 data buffers (now seeded by the loader's `temporal` block → DISCRETE cadence, ess-v9a.5).\n  - metadata: Dict(CoupleType => OpenAQCoupler, SysDomainInfo => domaininfo).\n\nData flow (upstream implementation, now performed by the runtime via the loader + cell-averaging regridder):\n  1. Station discovery: OpenAQ API v3 /locations query, bbox-filtered, parameter-filtered, paginated; cached to $EARTHSCIDATADIR/openaq_stations/{parameter}_{bbox}.json.\n  2. S3 download: asyncmap over (station, date) pairs; per-station daily CSV.gz cached to $EARTHSCIDATADIR/openaq_data/locationid=N/year=YYYY/month=MM/location-N-YYYYMMDD.csv.gz.\n  3. loadslice!: for each hourly time step, reads daily CSV caches, filters by parameter column, averages readings within the hour per station, then averages across all stations in each grid cell (the cell-averaging regrid), applies unit_scale (to_unit(unit_string)).\n  4. DataSetInterpolator + create_interp_equation: wraps the gridded hourly slices and produces the MTK observed equation.\n\ngt-p3ep resolution: the @register_symbolic interp_unsafe pattern is replaced by the data_loaders §8 mechanism. obs.{parameter} is the loader variable that the runtime aggregates from station observations and provides as a gridded hourly field. The model observed is a direct pass-through: pm25(t) ~ obs.pm25.\n\nReprojection (RFC §6 step 2): OpenAQ's station coordinates are geographic (longlat/WGS84), so the reprojection rule selected by convention is ESD reprojection/longlat.esm (esd-47z.1) — the IDENTITY transform (a no-op). Because this is a `points` loader whose native point set is resolved at runtime (station discovery), the loader carries no formal GDD `grid`; the geographic crs is recorded in the loader's metadata.native_crs for provenance and convention selection.\n\nRegridding (RFC §6 step 3 / §5.2): declared per variable in the model `regrid` block. All OpenAQ fields are scattered station observations → the cell_average kernel (ESD regridding/point_cell_average_regrid.esm, esd-47z.4): bin-average the stations falling within each target cell. `missing_value` 0.0 fills target cells that contain no station.\n\nNote on missing_value (carried from the pre-migration data_loaders.regridding.fill_value = 0.0): the upstream constructor default fill_value is 0.0 (not NaN/missing) because DataSetInterpolator's BSpline propagates NaN to the entire field; grid cells with no stations receive 0.0. Upstream TODO comment: switch to NaN when BSpline handling is improved. The pre-migration `extrapolation: \"clamp\"` knob has no analogue in the cell-averaging kernel (empty cells are filled with missing_value rather than extrapolated) and is dropped.\n\nNote on spatial_interp: :linear (default) uses full multilinear interpolation; :nearest uses nearest-grid + time-only linear interpolation (~8x speedup when queries are always at grid-point centres).\n\nSupported parameters and their OpenAQ API IDs: pm25(2), pm10(1), o3(3), no2(5), so2(4), co(6), bc(11), pm1(19), no(7), nox(8). All report in µg/m³ (converted to kg/m³ by the loader's unit_conversion 1e-9).\n\nCoordinate conventions:\n  - lon/lat: radians; the runtime cell-averaging regridder converts to degrees to bin station coordinates into the target grid cells.\n  - Surface observations: no lev parameter (2-D point data).\n\nCoupler identity: this model was serialized with the model-level field `coupletype: \"OpenAQCoupler\"`, the EarthSciMLBase `CoupleType` metadata tag naming the Julia coupler struct that `EarthSciMLBase.couple2` dispatches on to find this component's pairwise coupling rules. The esm schema defined `coupletype` only before 0.8.0 (\"informational label identifying this system's role in coupling\"); 0.8.0 removed it in favour of explicit coupling — `coupling` entries naming components directly, or `coupling_roles` + `coupling_import` in a coupling-library file (esm-spec §10.9–§10.11). esm 1.0.0 has no model-level coupler-identity field, so the tag is recorded here to keep it recoverable.\n\nRegridding intent: this model was serialized with the model-level `regrid` map, one entry per variable naming the kernel that transfers the loaded native-grid field onto the consuming model's grid. The esm schema defined `regrid` only before 0.8.0. esm 1.0.0 states (esm-spec §8.6) that a data source performs no regridding and that there is NO `Model.regrid` map: the carrier is the `variable_map` entry's `transform` field on the coupling edge that consumes the field (§10.4/§10.5) — an ordinary `aggregate` expression, typically an `apply_expression_template` invocation of an imported overlap-weight library. No such coupling edge exists in this document, so the per-variable kernel choice is recorded here verbatim to keep it recoverable. This is a demotion from a structured field to prose, not an equivalent — the transform expression still has to be authored on whichever coupling edge consumes these fields.\n\n  pm25: method cell_average — PM2.5 concentration. Scattered station observations → cell-averaging regridder (ESD regridding/point_cell_average_regrid.esm, esd-47z.4): bin-average stations within each target cell. Target cells with no station are filled with missing_value 0.0 (carried from the pre-migration fill_value 0.0).\n  pm10: method cell_average — PM10 concentration. Scattered station observations → cell-averaging regridder (esd-47z.4); empty target cells filled with missing_value 0.0.\n  o3: method cell_average — Ozone concentration. Scattered station observations → cell-averaging regridder (esd-47z.4); empty target cells filled with missing_value 0.0.\n  no2: method cell_average — Nitrogen dioxide concentration. Scattered station observations → cell-averaging regridder (esd-47z.4); empty target cells filled with missing_value 0.0.\n  so2: method cell_average — Sulfur dioxide concentration. Scattered station observations → cell-averaging regridder (esd-47z.4); empty target cells filled with missing_value 0.0.\n  co: method cell_average — Carbon monoxide concentration. Scattered station observations → cell-averaging regridder (esd-47z.4); empty target cells filled with missing_value 0.0.\n  bc: method cell_average — Black carbon concentration. Scattered station observations → cell-averaging regridder (esd-47z.4); empty target cells filled with missing_value 0.0.\n  pm1: method cell_average — PM1 concentration. Scattered station observations → cell-averaging regridder (esd-47z.4); empty target cells filled with missing_value 0.0.\n  no: method cell_average — Nitric oxide concentration. Scattered station observations → cell-averaging regridder (esd-47z.4); empty target cells filled with missing_value 0.0.\n  nox: method cell_average — Nitrogen oxides (NOx) concentration. Scattered station observations → cell-averaging regridder (esd-47z.4); empty target cells filled with missing_value 0.0."
      },
      "tolerance": {
        "rel": 1e-06
      },
      "variables": {
        "lon": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Longitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's longitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem. The runtime cell-averaging regridder converts radians to degrees to bin OpenAQ station coordinates into target grid cells."
        },
        "lat": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "rad",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "Latitude of the model grid point (radians). Coupled to the simulation domain's latitude coordinate via param_to_var when composed into a CoupledSystem. The runtime cell-averaging regridder converts radians to degrees to bin OpenAQ station coordinates into target grid cells."
        },
        "pm25": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "kg/m^3",
          "shape": [],
          "description": "Hourly-averaged PM2.5 concentration at the model grid point (kg/m³), aggregated from monitoring stations within the grid cell by the cell-averaging regridder and converted from µg/m³. Target cells with no stations receive missing_value (0.0; see `regrid`). Sourced from the loader field obs.pm25. Variable name matches the constructor parameter ('pm25' shown here as the representative case; other instantiations use the respective parameter name: pm10, o3, no2, so2, co, bc, pm1, no, nox — each available as obs.<var>).",
          "update": {
            "kind": "data",
            "source": "OpenAQ_obs",
            "from": {
              "file_variable": "value",
              "description": "PM2.5 particulate matter concentration. Raw CSV 'value' column in µg/m³ (filtered where 'parameter' column == 'pm25'); converted to kg/m³ (1 µg/m³ = 1×10⁻⁹ kg/m³). OpenAQ API parameter ID: 2."
            }
